# TypeScript Rules

## Type Definitions
- Use explicit type declarations
- Avoid using 'any' type
- Use interfaces and types appropriately
- Utilize generics

## Type Safety
- Enable strict mode
- Perform thorough null checks
- Use type guards
- Minimize type assertions

## Code Organization
- Place type definitions in types directory
- Separate common types into dedicated files
- Consider type reusability
- Use modular type structure

## Best Practices
- Use readonly properties
- Use union and intersection types appropriately
- Utilize type inference
- Fix type errors immediately

## Documentation
- Comment complex types
- Document type definitions
- Document API types
- Document type changes
